ntdll: point the Vulkan loader at Wine's own MoltenVK manifest on macOS.

Gcenx's macOS builds of Wine, which Kelter uses, ship MoltenVK's driver
manifest in share/vulkan/icd.d and carry a change in ntdll.so that sets
VK_DRIVER_FILES to that folder when none of the Vulkan loader's variables
is set. Kelter replaces ntdll.so in its graphics copies of Wine, so it has
to do the same; otherwise Vulkan finds no driver, and Steam's browser
(ANGLE with Vulkan) fails to create its graphics context and stays blank.

Reconstructed from the behaviour of Gcenx's ntdll.so (LGPL); upstream Wine
has no such code. For Wine 11.21 with Wine Staging 11.21 applied.
LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -398,6 +398,19 @@
         bin_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", BINDIR );
         data_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", DATADIR "/wine" );
         wineloader = build_path( ntdll_dir, "wine" );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        /* macOS builds ship MoltenVK's driver manifest in Wine's own
+         * share/vulkan/icd.d. Point the Vulkan loader there, unless the
+         * user chose the drivers. */
+        if (!getenv( "VK_DRIVER_FILES" ) && !getenv( "VK_ICD_FILENAMES" ) && !getenv( "VK_ADD_DRIVER_FILES" ))
+        {
+            char *icd_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", DATADIR "/vulkan/icd.d" );
+            struct stat st;
+
+            if (!stat( icd_dir, &st ) && S_ISDIR( st.st_mode )) setenv( "VK_DRIVER_FILES", icd_dir, 1 );
+            free( icd_dir );
+        }
+#endif
     }
 
     set_dll_path();
